 = \\\\ (5\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5})-2\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ (5+3)\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 8\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df44ef82-3c73-5b75-bc3d-d84c7c1380c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df44ef82-3c73-5b75-bc3d-d84c7c1380c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "df44ef82-3c73-5b75-bc3d-d84c7c1380c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f797177-d53a-5907-82e8-bb0f6bd637df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a25c76c2-2df2-5c95-a861-9dd96c3f4a8f" "answer-6c57493f-9a04-58df-b0f0-bbb6bc2ec0cc" "answer-c3fc03d7-9299-50fb-8795-b3487550b44a" "answer-89117265-7cab-503c-92af-f188b42f42c6" "answer-4f797177-d53a-5907-82e8-bb0f6bd637df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a25c76c2-2df2-5c95-a861-9dd96c3f4a8f" :answer/id #uuid "a25c76c2-2df2-5c95-a861-9dd96c3f4a8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c57493f-9a04-58df-b0f0-bbb6bc2ec0cc" :answer/id #uuid "6c57493f-9a04-58df-b0f0-bbb6bc2ec0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3fc03d7-9299-50fb-8795-b3487550b44a" :answer/id #uuid "c3fc03d7-9299-50fb-8795-b3487550b44a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89117265-7cab-503c-92af-f188b42f42c6" :answer/id #uuid "89117265-7cab-503c-92af-f188b42f42c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f797177-d53a-5907-82e8-bb0f6bd637df" :answer/id #uuid "4f797177-d53a-5907-82e8-bb0f6bd637df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ea12d57-149c-5e75-92c8-881bf2f1c4e9" :question/id #uuid "5ea12d57-149c-5e75-92c8-881bf2f1c4e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-134567" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{7}+5\\sqrt[3]{162}-\\sqrt[3]{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{162} & =\\sqrt[3]{27\\cdot 6}=\\sqrt[3]{27}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6}=3\\sqrt[3]{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7}+5\\sqrt[3]{162}-\\sqrt[3]{6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7}+5(3\\sqrt[3]{6})-\\sqrt[3]{6}= \\\\ \\sqrt{7}+15\\sqrt[3]{6}-\\sqrt[3]{6}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{6}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7}+15\\sqrt[3]{6}-\\sqrt[3]{6}= \\\\ \\sqrt{7}+(15\\sqrt[3]{6}-\\sqrt[3]{6}) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7}+(15-1)\\sqrt[3]{6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7}+14\\sqrt[3]{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-648d8aec-59b5-5928-b88a-f36a1aea213d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-648d8aec-59b5-5928-b88a-f36a1aea213d" :answer-field/id #uuid "648d8aec-59b5-5928-b88a-f36a1aea213d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ab91932-e355-5352-aba3-b6df560e9b3b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-90c5b765-e85d-55b5-bfdb-78a5e3f6f707" "answer-ebecd2a6-8dca-5397-bfd3-0a2018b2b27f" "answer-0ab91932-e355-5352-aba3-b6df560e9b3b" "answer-55572885-5954-5b49-bbf7-ae2b41c0b283" "answer-7451faf5-8af1-525e-8e9d-8f546d5c31b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c5b765-e85d-55b5-bfdb-78a5e3f6f707" :answer/id #uuid "90c5b765-e85d-55b5-bfdb-78a5e3f6f707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebecd2a6-8dca-5397-bfd3-0a2018b2b27f" :answer/id #uuid "ebecd2a6-8dca-5397-bfd3-0a2018b2b27f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab91932-e355-5352-aba3-b6df560e9b3b" :answer/id #uuid "0ab91932-e355-5352-aba3-b6df560e9b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}+14\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55572885-5954-5b49-bbf7-ae2b41c0b283" :answer/id #uuid "55572885-5954-5b49-bbf7-ae2b41c0b283" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}+18\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7451faf5-8af1-525e-8e9d-8f546d5c31b9" :answer/id #uuid "7451faf5-8af1-525e-8e9d-8f546d5c31b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}+2\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-589b43ec-34cc-5c99-9404-4a02a5e69293" :question/id #uuid "589b43ec-34cc-5c99-9404-4a02a5e69293" :question/math-academy-id "q-134564" :question/problem "Simplify $4\\sqrt[3]{500}+\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{500} & =\\sqrt[3]{125\\cdot 4}=\\sqrt[3]{125}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{4}=5\\sqrt[3]{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt[3]{500}+\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 4(5\\sqrt[3]{4})+\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 20\\sqrt[3]{4}+\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{4}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20\\sqrt[3]{4}+\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ (20\\sqrt[3]{4}+\\sqrt[3]{4})-\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ (20+1)\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 21\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf930231-9174-5665-b2ca-c6932f6a88a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf930231-9174-5665-b2ca-c6932f6a88a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf930231-9174-5665-b2ca-c6932f6a88a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e601af1-3e88-5fbe-ba65-a25c0f8a7dda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7709f1c-d64f-535c-bdca-965e218fce82" "answer-4e601af1-3e88-5fbe-ba65-a25c0f8a7dda" "answer-816719f9-fd7d-5be7-bd5d-0eb6da521c78" "answer-53dfe897-c9ef-5994-b809-12a2b1fe9e9e" "answer-1f21b191-5b62-5c0c-994b-82c06678781d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7709f1c-d64f-535c-bdca-965e218fce82" :answer/id #uuid "e7709f1c-d64f-535c-bdca-965e218fce82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\sqrt[3]{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e601af1-3e88-5fbe-ba65-a25c0f8a7dda" :answer/id #uuid "4e601af1-3e88-5fbe-ba65-a25c0f8a7dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-816719f9-fd7d-5be7-bd5d-0eb6da521c78" :answer/id #uuid "816719f9-fd7d-5be7-bd5d-0eb6da521c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53dfe897-c9ef-5994-b809-12a2b1fe9e9e" :answer/id #uuid "53dfe897-c9ef-5994-b809-12a2b1fe9e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f21b191-5b62-5c0c-994b-82c06678781d" :answer/id #uuid "1f21b191-5b62-5c0c-994b-82c06678781d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt[3]{4}-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074948 :tutorial/content "When dealing with sums of square roots, we can combine any terms with the same number under the square root symbol $\\sqrt{\\phantom 0}.$\n\nFor example, consider the following expression:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt 5 + 4\\sqrt 5\n$$\n\nRemember that $2\\sqrt 5$ and $4\\sqrt 5$ mean $2\\cdot\\sqrt 5$ and $4\\cdot\\sqrt 5,$ respectively. \n\nWe can simplify our expression by combining the two radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5}+4\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ (2+4)\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 6\\sqrt{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{7}-1\\cdot \\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ (2-1)\\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ 1\\cdot \\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHowever, we *cannot* combine terms when the numbers under the radical are different. For example, the expression\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt 3 + \\sqrt 5\n$$\n\ncannot be simplified because there is no way of combining $\\sqrt 3$ and $\\sqrt 5.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075012 :tutorial/content "Recall that the product rule for radicals states that\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{a\\cdot b} = \\sqrt{a}\\cdot \\sqrt{b}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are nonnegative numbers. \n\nWe can use the product rule for radicals to simplify some expressions. Let's see an example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075013 :tutorial/content "We can simplify cube root expressions in the same way as with square roots.\n\nFor example, consider the following expression:\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt[3]2 - 6\\sqrt[3] 2\n$$\n\nWe can simplify our expression by combining the two radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt[3]{2}-6\\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ (4-6)\\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt[3]{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAs with square roots, we *cannot* combine terms when the numbers under the radical are different. For example, the expression\n\n$$\n3\\sqrt[3] 2 + \\sqrt[3] 5\n$$\n\ncannot be simplified because there is no way of combining $\\sqrt[3] 2$ and $\\sqrt[3] 5.$\n\nFinally, it is not possible to combine square root and cube root terms -- not even if the numbers under the radical symbol are the same! For example, the expression\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt 2 + \\sqrt[3] 2\n$$\n\ncannot be simplified because there is no way of combining $\\sqrt 2$ and $\\sqrt[3] 2.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073921 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186100233 :answer-field/choices 17592186100234] [:db/retract 17592186100233 :answer-field/choices 17592186100236] [:db/retract 17592186100233 :answer-field/choices 17592186100237] [:db/retract 17592186100233 :answer-field/choices 17592186100238] {:db/id 17592186101011 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f98810bc-183c-5870-9d6b-3edb2448dbd3" "question-ba0bf3ae-2fd6-52ea-bcad-b5d5a3e42790"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101012 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4082ce79-1f09-55c7-aa8e-8877c477aa68"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101013 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-23b2c3db-685f-514d-a3c0-859f60e7e231" "question-34da0315-7401-50d5-a9e5-7e5606f6c11f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100602 :question/worked-solution "First, we write the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{0.2^5}{0.2^2} = 0.2^5 \\div 0.2^2\n$$\n\nNow, to divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0.2}^{5}÷{0.2}^{2}={0.2}^{5-2}={0.2}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101014 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4c73aa99-debd-5794-8ba7-65ccf58c6b12" "question-0c28763f-6ec1-59b6-a61c-8e135c29d4f7" "question-dade69e9-73ae-574b-b21e-ceb9971eb952" "question-3f475ee2-0efc-5b85-a0eb-323e7d9761d6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100603 :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{2^3}{2^5}.$" :question/worked-solution "To divide powers of the same base, we subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2^3}{2^5} = 2^{3-5} = 2^{-2}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate $2^{-2},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(2)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n2^{-2}  = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^2 =\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f98810bc-183c-5870-9d6b-3edb2448dbd3" :question/id #uuid "f98810bc-183c-5870-9d6b-3edb2448dbd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-68333" :question/problem "$\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{3}^{-3}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{3}^{-3}}={3}^{2}÷{3}^{-3}\n$$\n\nNow, to divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}÷{3}^{-3} & ={3}^{2-(-3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2+3} \\\\  & ={3}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a466f623-ab3b-5e98-a288-051d3f760179"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a466f623-ab3b-5e98-a288-051d3f760179" :answer-field/id #uuid "a466f623-ab3b-5e98-a288-051d3f760179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36d84933-4b30-552c-817e-4f84f2dfdaa4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04609a83-98ea-5468-ba34-1ed13fd5596b" "answer-409d7498-15a2-5844-8022-9593137205a2" "answer-304e1c7e-ff88-570e-8567-601be1b1cfe2" "answer-36d84933-4b30-552c-817e-4f84f2dfdaa4" "answer-efd8fd17-f486-52b1-9c78-d9c83ff1da63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04609a83-98ea-5468-ba34-1ed13fd5596b" :answer/id #uuid "04609a83-98ea-5468-ba34-1ed13fd5596b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-409d7498-15a2-5844-8022-9593137205a2" :answer/id #uuid "409d7498-15a2-5844-8022-9593137205a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{3}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-304e1c7e-ff88-570e-8567-601be1b1cfe2" :answer/id #uuid "304e1c7e-ff88-570e-8567-601be1b1cfe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{3}^{-2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36d84933-4b30-552c-817e-4f84f2dfdaa4" :answer/id #uuid "36d84933-4b30-552c-817e-4f84f2dfdaa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{3}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efd8fd17-f486-52b1-9c78-d9c83ff1da63" :answer/id #uuid "efd8fd17-f486-52b1-9c78-d9c83ff1da63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{6}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ba0bf3ae-2fd6-52ea-bcad-b5d5a3e42790" :question/id #uuid "ba0bf3ae-2fd6-52ea-bcad-b5d5a3e42790" :question/math-academy-id "q-72644" :question/problem "$(-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-2)^{3}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{(-2)^{7}}{(-2)^{3}} \\\\  & =(-2)^{7}÷(-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{7}÷(-2)^{3} & =(-2)^{7-3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-adb1e5ef-6744-5273-b11f-b1e143338675"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-adb1e5ef-6744-5273-b11f-b1e143338675" :answer-field/id #uuid "adb1e5ef-6744-5273-b11f-b1e143338675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbf75fb3-e091-53e6-a734-b0c3fdb293a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-208aacc2-c2ef-5d30-936c-23fe5a01dc2b" "answer-78ac69d7-4fb4-53e8-a972-8043fbc99ff2" "answer-bbf75fb3-e091-53e6-a734-b0c3fdb293a4" "answer-90cd3496-62c8-51c2-9150-37d7cc7d75c5" "answer-e9414fda-ce3b-5c86-a7a8-657ac7bbb3c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-208aacc2-c2ef-5d30-936c-23fe5a01dc2b" :answer/id #uuid "208aacc2-c2ef-5d30-936c-23fe5a01dc2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2)^{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ac69d7-4fb4-53e8-a972-8043fbc99ff2" :answer/id #uuid "78ac69d7-4fb4-53e8-a972-8043fbc99ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2)^{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbf75fb3-e091-53e6-a734-b0c3fdb293a4" :answer/id #uuid "bbf75fb3-e091-53e6-a734-b0c3fdb293a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2)^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90cd3496-62c8-51c2-9150-37d7cc7d75c5" :answer/id #uuid "90cd3496-62c8-51c2-9150-37d7cc7d75c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{2}^{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9414fda-ce3b-5c86-a7a8-657ac7bbb3c0" :answer/id #uuid "e9414fda-ce3b-5c86-a7a8-657ac7bbb3c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{2}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {