ac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{16}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-688e485a-87e1-5e22-8ef5-920c7f1b5542"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-688e485a-87e1-5e22-8ef5-920c7f1b5542" :answer-field/id #uuid "688e485a-87e1-5e22-8ef5-920c7f1b5542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-17e736bb-dd08-51b3-851b-0424dd8b1e5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4e0737a-c55a-53f1-8296-8cbdb2042a88" "answer-498857fc-e205-5e8c-81b2-ebd5d66bdab3" "answer-17e736bb-dd08-51b3-851b-0424dd8b1e5e" "answer-93fb7776-9234-5fcb-afe2-3a9bab6c861b" "answer-2258fd97-3bcf-5fa1-a22b-a31244e2527e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4e0737a-c55a-53f1-8296-8cbdb2042a88" :answer/id #uuid "e4e0737a-c55a-53f1-8296-8cbdb2042a88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-498857fc-e205-5e8c-81b2-ebd5d66bdab3" :answer/id #uuid "498857fc-e205-5e8c-81b2-ebd5d66bdab3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17e736bb-dd08-51b3-851b-0424dd8b1e5e" :answer/id #uuid "17e736bb-dd08-51b3-851b-0424dd8b1e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93fb7776-9234-5fcb-afe2-3a9bab6c861b" :answer/id #uuid "93fb7776-9234-5fcb-afe2-3a9bab6c861b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2258fd97-3bcf-5fa1-a22b-a31244e2527e" :answer/id #uuid "2258fd97-3bcf-5fa1-a22b-a31244e2527e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f475ee2-0efc-5b85-a0eb-323e7d9761d6" :question/id #uuid "3f475ee2-0efc-5b85-a0eb-323e7d9761d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-68123" :question/problem "$\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{6}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{6}}={5}^{4-6}={5}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${5}^{-2},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(5)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{5}^{-2}={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{1}{25}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0acca603-a05b-5f68-b892-8a15125bba86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0acca603-a05b-5f68-b892-8a15125bba86" :answer-field/id #uuid "0acca603-a05b-5f68-b892-8a15125bba86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3afa9deb-885c-52d6-a45d-127298fe4d1b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c18dd5a4-0919-5101-8048-855d479f3615" "answer-cdb1a1ec-60f2-58e1-a6d5-c32687beed48" "answer-3482c303-6fca-5901-852b-e619c98458ff" "answer-9ab0bb7b-86d9-51bf-88ed-98a433ac44e6" "answer-3afa9deb-885c-52d6-a45d-127298fe4d1b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c18dd5a4-0919-5101-8048-855d479f3615" :answer/id #uuid "c18dd5a4-0919-5101-8048-855d479f3615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdb1a1ec-60f2-58e1-a6d5-c32687beed48" :answer/id #uuid "cdb1a1ec-60f2-58e1-a6d5-c32687beed48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3482c303-6fca-5901-852b-e619c98458ff" :answer/id #uuid "3482c303-6fca-5901-852b-e619c98458ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ab0bb7b-86d9-51bf-88ed-98a433ac44e6" :answer/id #uuid "9ab0bb7b-86d9-51bf-88ed-98a433ac44e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{125}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3afa9deb-885c-52d6-a45d-127298fe4d1b" :answer/id #uuid "3afa9deb-885c-52d6-a45d-127298fe4d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102023 :tutorial/content "To divide powers of the same base, we simply *subtract* the exponents. This is known as the **quotient rule for exponents**. For instance, in the expression \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}3}^5 \\div {\\color{blue}3}^2,\n$$\n\nboth powers have the same base $({\\color{blue}3})$. Therefore, we can simplify this expression by subtracting the exponents:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}3}^5 \\div {\\color{blue}3}^2 = {\\color{blue}3}^{5-2} = {\\color{blue}3}^3.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The quotient rule for exponents is really just a quicker alternative to the following process:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{5}÷{3}^{2} & = \\\\ {3}^{3+2}÷{3}^{2} & = \\\\ {3}^{3}\\times {{{3}^{2}÷{3}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{=1} & = \\\\ {3}^{3}\\times 1 & = \\\\ {3}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102024 :tutorial/content "We can use the quotient rule for exponents with negative exponents too. For example, to simplify $3^{-5}\\div 3^{-3},$ we subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n3^{-5} \\div 3^{-3} = 3^{-5-(-3)} = 3^{-2}\n$$\n\nNow, to evaluate $3^{-2},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(3)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n3^{-2}  = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right)^2 =\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{9}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101075 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186067012 :answer-field/choices 17592186067013] [:db/retract 17592186067012 :answer-field/choices 17592186067014] [:db/retract 17592186067012 :answer-field/choices 17592186067015] [:db/retract 17592186067012 :answer-field/choices 17592186067016] [:db/retract 17592186067012 :answer-field/choices 17592186067017] {:db/id 17592186068761 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19e2fba4-263d-5d97-b42a-74a9677543ff" "question-055a4a11-a8c1-52ea-9a96-5ba018fca1a6" "question-b7b36623-4cad-581d-9fdb-5ce9b684b932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068599 :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-1 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}+x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}+3x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${\\color{blue}2x-1},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${\\color{red}3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068817 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-181fbf98-acb9-50e0-be18-f71c1745254f" "question-e87d282e-0d52-5290-b71b-daa1fd77975b" "question-50f23ba0-92ed-55f7-8001-c1ea7b79fdae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068762 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0aed3cc1-c2b0-58fe-afde-dbd43b0a8ab9" "question-081856a1-5ee4-5d5e-9555-d794c0719197" "question-09911eb6-f7c1-5633-957d-b9003c3e05af" "question-e0e14597-882f-5740-a997-7cf558df262d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068600 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^3$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n2x^4-7x^2-x+8 = 2x^4+{\\color{red}0}x^3-7x^2-x+8\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}+0x+5}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is ${2x^2 - 5},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${-x+3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 + \\dfrac{-x+3}{x^2-1}.\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 - \\dfrac{x-3}{x^2-1}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-19e2fba4-263d-5d97-b42a-74a9677543ff" :question/id #uuid "19e2fba4-263d-5d97-b42a-74a9677543ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-322775" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3{x}^{2}-5x+2$ | __ |  |  | $3{x}^{2}-5x+2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+15 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}-5x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{18{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+12x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,45{x}^{2}-65x+32 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,45{x}^{2}-75x+30}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,10x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $6x+15,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $10x+2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{18{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-53x+32}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}=6x+15+\\frac{10x+2}{3{x}^{2}-5x+2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5aece7f-4616-5dcd-a42e-331a18bbd733" "answer-field-3b46f401-635f-539a-b7a6-61f061a7d7cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5aece7f-4616-5dcd-a42e-331a18bbd733" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5aece7f-4616-5dcd-a42e-331a18bbd733" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8cbd5e88-4232-5919-892f-a641f432c3a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8cbd5e88-4232-5919-892f-a641f432c3a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cbd5e88-4232-5919-892f-a641f432c3a5" :answer/id #uuid "8cbd5e88-4232-5919-892f-a641f432c3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b46f401-635f-539a-b7a6-61f061a7d7cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b46f401-635f-539a-b7a6-61f061a7d7cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4d6c5488-8909-568f-a42e-e89e6b133cd8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d6c5488-8909-568f-a42e-e89e6b133cd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d6c5488-8909-568f-a42e-e89e6b133cd8" :answer/id #uuid "4d6c5488-8909-568f-a42e-e89e6b133cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069307 :question/problem "$\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6}{{x}^{2}+x+9}=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-3 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+x+9\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-3x-6 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-3x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $21.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6}{{x}^{2}+x+9}=x-3+\\frac{21}{{x}^{2}+x+9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067012 :answer-field/correct "answer-a894975e-16ab-5052-bdc4-b86ef962e5db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae7ace86-fe28-5ff6-952f-e50ef4a0d5cb" "answer-478bda68-4a2f-5923-b944-e44d5ec764c9" "answer-09119ba9-7069-5c48-9bf8-897c67cce065" "answer-d1558d43-d0e6-5519-bcfd-30ab9f190abf" "answer-a894975e-16ab-5052-bdc4-b86ef962e5db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae7ace86-fe28-5ff6-952f-e50ef4a0d5cb" :answer/id #uuid "ae7ace86-fe28-5ff6-952f-e50ef4a0d5cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+3+\\frac{13}{{x}^{2}+x+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-478bda68-4a2f-5923-b944-e44d5ec764c9" :answer/id #uuid "478bda68-4a2f-5923-b944-e44d5ec764c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-3+\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+x+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09119ba9-7069-5c48-9bf8-897c67cce065" :answer/id #uuid "09119ba9-7069-5c48-9bf8-897c67cce065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-1+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}+x+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1558d43-d0e6-5519-bcfd-30ab9f190abf" :answer/id #uuid "d1558d43-d0e6-5519-bcfd-30ab9f190abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3+\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+x+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a894975e-16ab-5052-bdc4-b86ef962e5db" :answer/id #uuid "a894975e-16ab-5052-bdc4-b86ef962e5db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3+\\frac{21}{{x}^{2}+x+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-055a4a11-a8c1-52ea-9a96-5ba018fca1a6" :question/id #uuid "055a4a11-a8c1-52ea-9a96-5ba018fca1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105586" :question/problem "What is the remainder when $3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-6x+2$ is divided by $3{x}^{2}-2x+1?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+3 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-6x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9{x}^{2}-7x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9{x}^{2}-6x+3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-x-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53d9a03f-d48f-58cb-b825-f2ee722c3226"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53d9a03f-d48f-58cb-b825-f2ee722c3226" :answer-field/id #uuid "53d9a03f-d48f-58cb-b825-f2ee722c3226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d49ecec8-c14f-5aba-a6d4-502f775afe38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d49ecec8-c14f-5aba-a6d4-502f775afe38" "answer-cab645fe-2a17-5552-9ea5-1134a9e3d8f1" "answer-ad4f0f20-94ac-5305-8dd3-f36fdad09d0e" "answer-be34c76d-bd07-5137-b154-241674337dbe" "answer-0f22a760-4eff-5fab-8cb2-c21e78e5614c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d49ecec8-c14f-5aba-a6d4-502f775afe38" :answer/id #uuid "d49ecec8-c14f-5aba-a6d4-502f775afe38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cab645fe-2a17-5552-9ea5-1134a9e3d8f1" :answer/id #uuid "cab645fe-2a17-5552-9ea5-1134a9e3d8f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad4f0f20-94ac-5305-8dd3-f36fdad09d0e" :answer/id #uuid "ad4f0f20-94ac-5305-8dd3-f36fdad09d0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be34c76d-bd07-5137-b154-241674337dbe" :answer/id #uuid "be34c76d-bd07-5137-b154-241674337dbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f22a760-4eff-5fab-8cb2-c21e78e5614c" :answer/id #uuid "0f22a760-4eff-5fab-8cb2-c21e78e5614c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186302125 :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+9 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-3x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,12{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}0{x}^{2}-20x+96\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{12{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+30x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,18{x}^{2}-50x+96 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,18{x}^{2}-27x+45}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-23x+51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $6x+9,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-23x+51.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12{x}^{3}-20x+96}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5}=6x+9+\\frac{(-23x+51)}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7b36623-4cad-581d-9fdb-5ce9b684b932" :question/id #uuid "b7b36623-4cad-581d-9fdb-5ce9b684b932" :question/math-academy-id "q-321932" :question/problem "What is the remainder when $4{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-35x+17$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-3x-10?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-3x-10\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-35x+17\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-40x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+5x+17 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}+3x+10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $4x-1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $2x+7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdde6b88-2bcb-59a9-a552-8cc51dc4dfa1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdde6b88-2bcb-59a9-a552-8cc51dc4dfa1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdde6b88-2bcb-59a9-a552-8cc51dc4dfa1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2915697b-699e-5131-b7a6-11d2d22e5d20" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2915697b-699e-5131-b7a6-11d2d22e5d20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2915697b-699e-5131-b7a6-11d2d22e5d20" :answer/id #uuid "2915697b-699e-5131-b7a6-11d2d22e5d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-181fbf98-acb9-50e0-be18-f71c1745254f" :question/id #uuid "181fbf98-acb9-50e0-be18-f71c1745254f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105619" :question/problem "What is the quotient of $2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x+2$ divided by ${x}^{2}-x+3?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}-x+3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $2{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-010cb54c-0f9d-56c9-9967-ad2ac4ae38eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-010cb54c-0f9d-56c9-9967-ad2ac4ae38eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "010cb54c-0f9d-56c9-9967-ad2ac4ae38eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-31d3149e-62e0-5553-8a53-0780ff5bea82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31d3149e-62e0-5553-8a53-0780ff5bea82" "answer-517bd432-634c-5160-a7c1-2798b49ac31f" "answer-47e6fbc6-16ce-5c95-b3e2-0c7ae79faa24" "answer-0734a952-dc65-5b73-a0ac-42bb5c00de1e" "answer-2106ff9c-2d6f-57eb-b089-6338b3cf678d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31d3149e-62e0-5553-8a53-0780ff5bea82" :answer/id #uuid "31d3149e-62e0-5553-8a53-0780ff5bea82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-517bd432-634c-5160-a7c1-2798b49ac31f" :answer/id #uuid "517bd432-634c-5160-a7c1-2798b49ac31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47e6fbc6-16ce-5c95-b3e2-0c7ae79faa24" :answer/id #uuid "47e6fbc6-16ce-5c95-b3e2-0c7ae79faa24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0734a952-dc65-5b73-a0ac-42bb5c00de1e" :answer/id #uuid "0734a952-dc65-5b73-a0ac-42bb5c00de1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2106ff9c-2d6f-57eb-b089-6338b3cf678d" :answer/id #uuid "2106ff9c-2d6f-57eb-b089-6338b3cf678d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186302177 :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x+1 \\\\  & 3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+5x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-\\phantom{0}8{x}^{2}+6x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,-\\,6{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\,2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+5x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-7x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the quotient is $-2x+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $4{x}^{2}-7x+6.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186301270 :answer-field/correct "answer-35ab54f6-7707-5402-80d0-dc69bbc677d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35ab54f6-7707-5402-80d0-dc69bbc677d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35ab54f6-7707-5402-80d0-dc69bbc677d4" :answer/id #uuid "35ab54f6-7707-5402-80d0-dc69bbc677d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x^{2}-7x+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e87d282e-0d52-5290-b71b-daa1fd77975b" :question/id #uuid "e87d282e-0d52-5290-b71b-daa1fd77975b" :question/math-academy-id "q-325109" :question/problem "What is the remainder of $-8{x}^{4}+18{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-12x+8$ divided by $2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+x+5?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4x+3 \\\\  & 2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-8{x}^{4}+18{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-12x+\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,-\\,8{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+8x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+3x+15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $5x-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe3adf2d-5dd2-5bae-9739-e53579bef45b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe3adf2d-5dd2-5bae-9739-e53579bef45b" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe3adf2d-5dd2-5bae-9739-e53579bef45b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e9cd52c7-ae5b-5a9d-99b9-ae90c2a70d70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9cd52c7-ae5b-5a9d-99b9-ae90c2a70d70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9cd52c7-ae5b-5a9d-99b9-ae90c2a70d70" :answer/id #uuid "e9cd52c7-ae5b-5a9d-99b9-ae90c2a70d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-50f23ba0-92ed-55f7-8001-c1ea7b79fdae" :question/id #uuid "50f23ba0-92ed-55f7-8001-c1ea7b79fdae" :question/math-academy-id "q-270162" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-6{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-10}{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $-6{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-10$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2$ | __ |  |  | $2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3x-4 \\\\  & 2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{4}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{3}-\\phantom{0}2{x}^{2}+\\phantom{00}x-10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-\\,6{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}-5x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-\\,8{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-16x+8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,2{x}^{2}+11x-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $-3x-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-2{x}^{2}+11x-18.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-10}{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2} & =-3x-4+\\frac{(-2{x}^{2}+11x-18)}{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6a6f954-cc7f-5c76-abb2-676e04e4d6bc" "answer-field-c4ada65e-58e7-559a-beba-d26715127a20"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6a6f954-cc7f-5c76-abb2-676e04e4d6bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a6f954-cc7f-5c76-abb2-676e04e4d6bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-aac526c4-f867-521e-a7e6-3e043c31ec08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aac526c4-f867-521e-a7e6-3e043c31ec08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aac526c4-f867-521e-a7e6-3e043c31ec08" :answer/id #uuid "aac526c4-f867-521e-a7e6-3e043c31ec08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4ada65e-58e7-559a-beba-d26715127a20" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ada65e-58e7-559a-beba-d26715127a20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e056ca2c-08b9-5433-8225-0a719c3ef8e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e056ca2c-08b9-5433-8225-0a719c3ef8e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e056ca2c-08b9-5433-8225-0a719c3ef8e3" :answer/id #uuid "e056ca2c-08b9-5433-8225-0a719c3ef8e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x^{2}+11x-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0aed3cc1-c2b0-58fe-afde-dbd43b0a8ab9" :question/id #uuid "0aed3cc1-c2b0-58fe-afde-dbd43b0a8ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-325144" :question/problem "What is the remainder of $-4{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-9$ divided by ${x}^{2}-2x+3?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-9=-4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}-8x-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-\\phantom{00}{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}0x-\\phantom{0}9\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8{x}^{3}+11{x}^{2}+0x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}-24x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}+24x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-5{x}^{2}+10x-15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,14x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-4{x}^{2}-8x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $14x+6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e76a0f26-821e-5882-8ff1-70b08ab07b0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e76a0f26-821e-5882-8ff1-70b08ab07b0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e76a0f26-821e-5882-8ff1-70b08ab07b0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3fea29c4-724d-5592-acaa-fa8c9360ef14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fea29c4-724d-5592-acaa-fa8c9360ef14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fea29c4-724d-5592-acaa-fa8c9360ef14" :answer/id #uuid "3fea29c4-724d-5592-acaa-fa8c9360ef14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14x+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186302185 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{3}+16=-4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+16\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-3 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-3x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}0x+6\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-6{x}^{2}+10x+16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,6{x}^{2}+9x-15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-2x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+31.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-081856a1-5ee4-5d5e-9555-d794c0719197" :question/id #uuid "081856a1-5ee4-5d5e-9555-d794c0719197" :question/math-academy-id "q-114524" :question/problem "$\\frac{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1={x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+2x\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & {x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}+0{x}^{2}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2x+0}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}+2x,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} \\\\ .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-12f76e1a-9a3d-5ac6-bfbf-3674987fa283"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12f76e1a-9a3d-5ac6-bfbf-3674987fa283" :answer-field/id #uuid "12f76e1a-9a3d-5ac6-bfbf-3674987fa283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee3ed9c8-febc-5465-8a71-f9072050b20c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee3ed9c8-febc-5465-8a71-f9072050b20c" "answer-9576bb1b-4a4e-5873-90a7-bbd7c225f503" "answer-9ae7fcb4-3a41-50f8-98a8-794d4f79c750" "answer-f7ddbe3a-e66f-5392-b989-1e189e9be995" "answer-0a078755-5f4a-57c8-926a-232b6508dd5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee3ed9c8-febc-5465-8a71-f9072050b20c" :answer/id #uuid "ee3ed9c8-febc-5465-8a71-f9072050b20c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9576bb1b-4a4e-5873-90a7-bbd7c225f503" :answer/id #uuid "9576bb1b-4a4e-5873-90a7-bbd7c225f503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ae7fcb4-3a41-50f8-98a8-794d4f79c750" :answer/id #uuid "9ae7fcb4-3a41-50f8-98a8-794d4f79c750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x-1+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7ddbe3a-e66f-5392-b989-1e189e9be995" :answer/id #uuid "f7ddbe3a-e66f-5392-b989-1e189e9be995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x-1-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a078755-5f4a-57c8-926a-232b6508dd5e" :answer/id #uuid "0a078755-5f4a-57c8-926a-232b6508dd5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-09911eb6-f7c1-5633-957d-b9003c3e05af" :question/id #uuid "09911eb6-f7c1-5633-957d-b9003c3e05af" :question/math-academy-id "q-324442" :question/problem "What is the remainder of $-2{x}^{3}-8$ divided by $-{x}^{2}+2x-3?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{3}-8=-2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-8\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+4 \\\\  & -{x}^{2}+2x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}+6x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-4{x}^{2}+8x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,2x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $2x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-2x+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b5296c6-8466-5ac4-ae38-14da36126aa8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b5296c6-8466-5ac4-ae38-14da36126aa8" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5296c6-8466-5ac4-ae38-14da36126aa8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fdf31618-0080-5092-b97f-1983fd960faa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdf31618-0080-5092-b97f-1983fd960faa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdf31618-0080-5092-b97f-1983fd960faa" :answer/id #uuid "fdf31618-0080-5092-b97f-1983fd960faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0e14597-882f-5740-a997-7cf558df262d" :question/id #uuid "e0e14597-882f-5740-a997-7cf558df262d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114523" :question/problem "What is the remainder when $3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-1$ is divided by $3{x}^{2}+2x-1?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-1=3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+2 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}+2x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{ }6{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}+4x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-4x+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-092b7512-31b4-5a29-bf6c-0f1cca26713c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-092b7512-31b4-5a29-bf6c-0f1cca26713c" :answer-field/id #uuid "092b7512-31b4-5a29-bf6c-0f1cca26713c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-02c9aef9-8d56-536c-ad1a-eb90516a9b6f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02c9aef9-8d56-536c-ad1a-eb90516a9b6f" "answer-b8e776e2-99e2-59fa-8d6c-567b839a4af9" "answer-795d8634-6770-5957-a96e-73e55b38e58d" "answer-4b2dda59-97b3-52ee-81d9-8f054c2d2d17" "answer-d3ce406c-15be-5d89-a8b8-a32986a9e199"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02c9aef9-8d56-536c-ad1a-eb90516a9b6f" :answer/id #uuid "02c9aef9-8d56-536c-ad1a-eb90516a9b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8e776e2-99e2-59fa-8d6c-567b839a4af9" :answer/id #uuid "b8e776e2-99e2-59fa-8d6c-567b839a4af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-795d8634-6770-5957-a96e-73e55b38e58d" :answer/id #uuid "795d8634-6770-5957-a96e-73e55b38e58d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b2dda59-97b3-52ee-81d9-8f054c2d2d17" :answer/id #uuid "4b2dda59-97b3-52ee-81d9-8f054c2d2d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3ce406c-15be-5d89-a8b8-a32986a9e199" :answer/id #uuid "d3ce406c-15be-5d89-a8b8-a32986a9e199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069974 :tutorial/content "The long division method allows us to divide a polynomial by another nonlinear polynomial.\n\nFor example, suppose we want to find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-4x^3+4x^2+x+4}{4x^2-1}\n$$\n\nHere, the divisor is the quadratic polynomial $4x^2-1$. \n\nAgain, we follow a step-by-step process.\n\n**Step 1**\n\nWe start by writing the dividend and the divisor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**\n\nWe divide the leading term of the dividend $({\\color{red}{-4x^3}})$ by the leading term of the divisor $({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}).$ This gives $\\left(\\dfrac{\\color{red}{-4x^3}}{{\\color{blue}{4x^2}}}\\right)={\\color{#8b008b}{-x}}.$ We add this result to the quotient line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the $\\color{#8b008b}-x$ we just found by the full divisor ${\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1.$ This gives ${\\color{#8b008b}-x}({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1)=-4x^3+x.$ We place this underneath the dividend, being sure to match the terms. Notice that we include a zero coefficient for the $x^2$ term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we subtract $-4x^3+0x^2+x$ from $-4x^3+4x^2+x+4$ and get $4x^2+0x+4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**\n\nWe now repeat the process. The new dividend is ${\\color{red}{4x^2}}+0x+4.$\n\nWe divide the leading term of the dividend $({\\color{red}{4x^2}})$ by the leading term of the divisor $({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}).$ This gives $\\left(\\dfrac{{\\color{red}{4x^2}}}{{\\color{blue}{4x^2}}}\\right)={\\color{#8b008b}{1}}.$ We  add this result to the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the ${\\color{#8b008b}{1}}$ we just found by the full divisor ${\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1.$ This gives ${\\color{#8b008b}{1}}({\\color{blue}{4x^2}}-1)=4x^2-1.$ We place this result underneath the dividend:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+0x-1}_{―}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract $4x^2+0x-1$ from $4x^2+0x+4$ to get ${\\color{red}{5}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+1 \\\\  & 4{x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+0x-1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're left with the constant $\\color{red}5$, which has a smaller degree than the divisor. So, the division is complete.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n- the quotient of the polynomial division is ${\\color{blue}{-x+1}},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${\\color{red}{5}}.$\n\nOur complete result can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4x^3+4x^2+x+4}{4x^2-1}={\\color{blue}{-x+1}} + \\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{4x^2-1}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068960 :activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172006 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-99aa1c5a-eed9-5ae6-b8c6-e2b13db7c0f6" "question-b831793d-1ec0-54c8-869c-6f86de445418"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-99aa1c5a-eed9-5ae6-b8c6-e2b13db7c0f6" :question/id #uuid "99aa1c5a-eed9-5ae6-b8c6-e2b13db7c0f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96367" :question/problem "Mark runs a hotel near a popular tourist resort. He knows that, on average, people usually book their room $3.5$ days before their trip. By modeling the number of days between the customer's booking and arrival as continuous and assuming that these numbers are independent, determine the probability that the next customer books their room less than $1$ full day in advance. Round your answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Since the time interval between the customer's booking and arrival is continuous and the time of different bookings are independent and occur at a constant average rate, we can model the time between the next customer's booking and arrival using an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of days between a booking and the customer's arrival. Since customers book their room $3.5=7/2$ days in advance on average, $X$ can be modeled as an exponential random variable with rate $\\lambda =2/7,$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{2}{7}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{7}{e}^{-2x/7}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a customer books a room less than $1$ full day in advance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{7}{e}^{-2x/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x/7}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2/7}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.2485\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a99fb244-28cb-58fa-857b-0ab86cacbcc2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a99fb244-28cb-58fa-857b-0ab86cacbcc2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a99fb244-28cb-58fa-857b-0ab86cacbcc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f7f8381-9c80-59cc-9eb2-c3583a9235be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e33eb3c-cec7-5493-9f32-c984010c4bb5" "answer-8f7f8381-9c80-59cc-9eb2-c3583a9235be" "answer-c29e1a84-9ffd-505b-8a79-6dcd87d514f1" "answer-e3ea36b6-b0d0-5067-953e-f4ef81d92a91" "answer-275b76d2-5fd6-553c-b3f2-cd785fa8f998"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e33eb3c-cec7-5493-9f32-c984010c4bb5" :answer/id #uuid "1e33eb3c-cec7-5493-9f32-c984010c4bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0302" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f7f8381-9c80-59cc-9eb2-c3583a9235be" :answer/id #uuid "8f7f8381-9c80-59cc-9eb2-c3583a9235be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2485" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c29e1a84-9ffd-505b-8a79-6dcd87d514f1" :answer/id #uuid "c29e1a84-9ffd-505b-8a79-6dcd87d514f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4353" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3ea36b6-b0d0-5067-953e-f4ef81d92a91" :answer/id #uuid "e3ea36b6-b0d0-5067-953e-f4ef81d92a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7515" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-275b76d2-5fd6-553c-b3f2-cd785fa8f998" :answer/id #uuid "275b76d2-5fd6-553c-b3f2-cd785fa8f998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9670" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172637 :question/worked-solution "Since the time until the next call is answered occurs continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next call is answered using an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the time, in minutes, between calls. Then, since there are $3$ calls per minute on average, the rate is $\\lambda =3$ calls per minute.\n\nThe amount of time before the next call can be modeled as an exponential random variable with rate $\\lambda =3,$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(3).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the next call will occur after $1$ minute or more is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }3{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\infty }+{e}^{-3} \\\\  & =0+{e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3} \\\\  & ≈0.0498.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171447 :answer-field/correct 17592186171450 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b831793d-1ec0-54c8-869c-6f86de445418" :question/id #uuid "b831793d-1ec0-54c8-869c-6f86de445418" :question/math-academy-id "q-132546" :question/problem "Vehicles arrive at a crossing continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of one every $10$ seconds. Determine the probability that the next vehicle will arrive at the crossing within the next $3$ seconds. Round your answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Since the time intervals between the arrival of two successive vehicles at the crossing are continuous and independent, and arrivals occur at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next vehicle arrives as an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the time between the arrival of two successive vehicles at the crossing. Then, since vehicles arrive every $10$ seconds on average, the rate is $\\lambda =1/10$ vehicles per second.\n\nThe time between arrivals can be modeled as an exponential random variable with rate $\\lambda =1/10,$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{10}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}{e}^{-x/10}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the next vehicle will arrive at the crossing within the next $3$ seconds is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{10}{e}^{-x/10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-{e}^{-x/10}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3/10}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3/10} \\\\  & ≈0.2592\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd2f20a1-a54d-5ed7-a2a8-fb23d83de889"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd2f20a1-a54d-5ed7-a2a8-fb23d83de889" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2f20a1-a54d-5ed7-a2a8-fb23d83de889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c54cf95-8d93-5f06-addc-038acebc5019" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48a6a32b-b9ab-5bec-85a1-8073a3608631" "answer-5814f8c1-9cae-53cc-8145-d58f8cc938cb" "answer-0c54cf95-8d93-5f06-addc-038acebc5019" "answer-668716e1-89c4-559b-bcb0-1a077d43cacc" "answer-0c65b508-2845-571b-8454-76c6030fae62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48a6a32b-b9ab-5bec-85a1-8073a3608631" :answer/id #uuid "48a6a32b-b9ab-5bec-85a1-8073a3608631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2529" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5814f8c1-9cae-53cc-8145-d58f8cc938cb" :answer/id #uuid "5814f8c1-9cae-53cc-8145-d58f8cc938cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2552" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c54cf95-8d93-5f06-addc-038acebc5019" :answer/id #uuid "0c54cf95-8d93-5f06-addc-038acebc5019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2592" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-668716e1-89c4-559b-bcb0-1a077d43cacc" :answer/id #uuid "668716e1-89c4-559b-bcb0-1a077d43cacc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2599" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c65b508-2845-571b-8454-76c6030fae62" :answer/id #uuid "0c65b508-2845-571b-8454-76c6030fae62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2952" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172008 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b588bb0d-6d8e-5a2d-ae2c-642f8c01ed06"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172532 :question/problem "At a particular helpdesk, customer waiting times occur continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of $6$ customers per hour. If a customer has already waited for $6$ minutes, what is the probability that they will need to wait at least $4$ more minutes for their call to be answered? Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\nThe required probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since waiting times occur continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next call is answered using an exponential distribution.\n\nLet $X$ be the customer's waiting time, in minutes. Since the help desk serves $6$ customers per hour on average (or $1$ customer every $10$ minutes), the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{10}$ customers per minute, and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{10}).\n$$\n\nRecall that exponential random variables have the memoryless property. So, given two positive real numbers $s,t,$ we have that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{10},$ $s=6,$ and $t=4.$ \n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6+4\\,|\\,X>6) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(1/10)\\cdot (4)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2/5} \\\\  & ≈0.670.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186170847 :answer-field/correct "answer-87cb0385-7440-5272-98a7-928a22fd8042" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87cb0385-7440-5272-98a7-928a22fd8042"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87cb0385-7440-5272-98a7-928a22fd8042" :answer/id #uuid "87cb0385-7440-5272-98a7-928a22fd8042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.670" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b588bb0d-6d8e-5a2d-ae2c-642f8c01ed06" :question/id #uuid "b588bb0d-6d8e-5a2d-ae2c-642f8c01ed06" :question/math-academy-id "q-254586" :question/problem "A fisherman catches fish continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of $1$ fish every $15$ minutes. If the fisherman has already been fishing for $30$ minutes without catching any fish, what is the probability that he will need to fish for at least $20$ more minutes before catching his first fish? Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\nThe required probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since catching fish occurs continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next catch using an exponential distribution.\n\nLet $X$ be the time until the next catch, in minutes. Since the fisherman catches $1$ fish every $15$ minutes on average, the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{15}$ fish per minute, and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{15}).\n$$\n\nRecall that exponential random variables have the memoryless property. So, given two positive real numbers $s,t,$ we have that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{15},$ $s=30,$ and $t=20.$ \n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>30+20\\,|\\,X>30) & =P(X>20) \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(1/15)\\cdot (20)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4/3} \\\\  & ≈0.264.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-938386cd-7f18-57c1-8aef-c0067eb1a186"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-938386cd-7f18-57c1-8aef-c0067eb1a186" :answer-field/id #uuid "938386cd-7f18-57c1-8aef-c0067eb1a186" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5baebaba-fb25-532c-a3b0-5a6c14ea2ee8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5baebaba-fb25-532c-a3b0-5a6c14ea2ee8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5baebaba-fb25-532c-a3b0-5a6c14ea2ee8" :answer/id #uuid "5baebaba-fb25-532c-a3b0-5a6c14ea2ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.264" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-616b3a6a-2237-5567-8bd3-bad7d041996f" :activity/id #uuid "616b3a6a-2237-5567-8bd3-bad7d041996f" :activity/title "Modeling With the Exponential Distribution" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048224 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-81c056b4-eadd-5982-a819-4d1188c88ca4" "step-362e8628-dbd8-5502-bb8d-0fc43dd4f500" "step-ce0bc65b-a275-58a3-b6a0-d989f4a9ad43" "step-48f1bc6d-2333-56a9-97a8-8077e356fb41" "step-9424cb41-3dfd-528c-948b-f29f36193749"] :activity/first-step "step-81c056b4-eadd-5982-a819-4d1188c88ca4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-81c056b4-eadd-5982-a819-4d1188c88ca4" :step/id #uuid "81c056b4-eadd-5982-a819-4d1188c88ca4" :step/content "question-99aa1c5a-eed9-5ae6-b8c6-e2b13db7c0f6" :step/next "step-362e8628-dbd8-5502-bb8d-0fc43dd4f500" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-362e8628-dbd8-5502-bb8d-0fc43dd4f500" :step/id #uuid "362e8628-dbd8-5502-bb8d-0fc43dd4f500" :step/content 17592186172637 :step/next "step-ce0bc65b-a275-58a3-b6a0-d989f4a9ad43" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ce0bc65b-a275-58a3-b6a0-d989f4a9ad43" :step/id #uuid "ce0bc65b-a275-58a3-b6a0-d989f4a9ad43" :step/content "question-b831793d-1ec0-54c8-869c-6f86de445418" :step/next "step-48f1bc6d-2333-56a9-97a8-8077e356fb41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-48f1bc6d-2333-56a9-97a8-8077e356fb41" :step/id #uuid "48f1bc6d-2333-56a9-97a8-8077e356fb41" :step/content 17592186172532 :step/next "step-9424cb41-3dfd-528c-948b-f29f36193749" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9424cb41-3dfd-528c-948b-f29f36193749" :step/id #uuid "9424cb41-3dfd-528c-948b-f29f36193749" :step/content "question-b588bb0d-6d8e-5a2d-ae2c-642f8c01ed06" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186131491 :answer-field/choices 17592186131492] [:db/retract 17592186131491 :answer-field/choices 17592186131493] [:db/retract 17592186131491 :answer-field/choices 17592186131494] [:db/retract 17592186131491 :answer-field/choices 17592186131495] [:db/retract 17592186131491 :answer-field/choices 17592186131496] [:db/retract 17592186131503 :answer-field/choices 17592186131504] [:db/retract 17592186131503 :answer-field/choices 17592186131506] [:db/retract 17592186131509 :answer-field/choices 17592186131511] [:db/retract 17592186131509 :answer-field/choices 17592186131513] [:db/retract 17592186131509 :answer-field/choices 17592186131514] {:db/id 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bb8ec734-9246-5393-99e6-34bea8046fc0" "question-83aaff63-f033-5323-bd52-af10976e5a16" "question-46db878d-0e5d-50fb-979a-d499bbe2ee60" "question-203918fb-bff3-5640-9116-ee4c833a081b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133503 :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc96a7656f4725f266f66c74752504b9b926b21215899cb4e62548f5c748ce4e.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A \\cdot A^T = I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA \\cdot A^T = A^T\\cdot A = I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n![](images/c7/c7cae63465ded2fe22d8ad21e22458042b3324f820ce2efcbe80df061cfecaeb.svg)\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A\\cdot A^T = I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-340e44da-12e6-5ccb-a96a-bc97b2d0d915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133505 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix ![](images/37/37ca77e520fc9797f39e3fb8d381c359a6c7f6f251d17de6ef9586968d5d0d0b.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-36bba55d-9122-58f3-aa1e-57a8674f5e02"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133504 :question/problem "![](images/d9/d97da6252422d33ef758793ec93d4ef85076fbaa524215ad19c709f42005aeff.svg)\n\nFind $|\\textrm{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35c37699-f2ab-5493-8b62-dd508d98be99" "question-4cd1f663-1b26-5239-80df-41dfbaf9dd53"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133506 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\nI. $2Q$ is orthogonal\n\nII. $P^{-1}Q$ is orthogonal\n\nIII. $PQ^T$ is orthogonal" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb8ec734-9246-5393-99e6-34bea8046fc0" :question/id #uuid "bb8ec734-9246-5393-99e6-34bea8046fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177661" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6f1d3ef9-793b-5e24-8e99-68db383cf524"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f1d3ef9-793b-5e24-8e99-68db383cf524" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f1d3ef9-793b-5e24-8e99-68db383cf524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d001edcd-7aa6-5ff6-a64d-f2057575b857" "answer-eeb3e8ee-7783-5420-882a-066010a26592" "answer-2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" "answer-658947d8-f94a-5959-8f98-7a5a5937a024" "answer-c5808f66-f6df-524e-9eaa-c92ca8711d50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d001edcd-7aa6-5ff6-a64d-f2057575b857" :answer/id #uuid "d001edcd-7aa6-5ff6-a64d-f2057575b857" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eeb3e8ee-7783-5420-882a-066010a26592" :answer/id #uuid "eeb3e8ee-7783-5420-882a-066010a26592" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer/id #uuid "2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-658947d8-f94a-5959-8f98-7a5a5937a024" :answer/id #uuid "658947d8-f94a-5959-8f98-7a5a5937a024" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5808f66-f6df-524e-9eaa-c92ca8711d50" :answer/id #uuid "c5808f66-f6df-524e-9eaa-c92ca8711d50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83aaff63-f033-5323-bd52-af10976e5a16" :question/id #uuid "83aaff63-f033-5323-bd52-af10976e5a16" :question/math-academy-id "q-177656" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d87ebbb7-74a3-5ba5-93e4-063a3206f479"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d87ebbb7-74a3-5ba5-93e4-063a3206f479" :answer-field/id #uuid "d87ebbb7-74a3-5ba5-93e4-063a3206f479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer-field/choices ["answer-013b5339-64c6-5007-b26d-8e17a9af1e89" "answer-a1ab3e2b-fed0-5981-a65e-df0e8c2ddfca" "answer-7c5f1870-fd22-5be7-af97-1d34504dc1ea" "answer-e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" "answer-eede04ef-d603-58e9-897e-2826d2f2ca05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-013b5339-64c6-5007-b26d-8e17a9af1e89" :answer/id #uuid "013b5339-64c6-5007-b26d-8e17a9af1e89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1ab3e2b-fed0-5981-a65e-df0e8c2ddfca" :answer/id #uuid "a1ab3e2b-fed0-5981-a65e-df0e8c2ddfca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c5f1870-fd22-5be7-af97-1d34504dc1ea" :answer/id #uuid "7c5f1870-fd22-5be7-af97-1d34504dc1ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer/id #uuid "e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eede04ef-d603-58e9-897e-2826d2f2ca05" :answer/id #uuid "eede04ef-d603-58e9-897e-2826d2f2ca05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46db878d-0e5d-50fb-979a-d499bbe2ee60" :question/id #uuid "46db878d-0e5d-50fb-979a-d499bbe2ee60" :question/math-academy-id "q-177659" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{24}{25} \\\\ \\frac{24}{25} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9f3276f-779b-51ad-9d6b-890a9e89a2ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9f3276f-779b-51ad-9d6b-890a9e89a2ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f3276f-779b-51ad-9d6b-890a9e89a2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0fff5188-49f9-5ba0-bde2-420c0a8bf40b" "answer-fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" "answer-65bb6b5a-1475-52a9-b0fc-a90761104b13" "answer-74086728-2a15-558c-9eda-23ae9a3e855c" "answer-5ceae71f-3b25-523c-b399-ef203fc61915"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fff5188-49f9-5ba0-bde2-420c0a8bf40b" :answer/id #uuid "0fff5188-49f9-5ba0-bde2-420c0a8bf40b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer/id #uuid "fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65bb6b5a-1475-52a9-b0fc-a90761104b13" :answer/id #uuid "65bb6b5a-1475-52a9-b0fc-a90761104b13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74086728-2a15-558c-9eda-23ae9a3e855c" :answer/id #uuid "74086728-2a15-558c-9eda-23ae9a3e855c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ceae71f-3b25-523c-b399-ef203fc61915" :answer/id #uuid "5ceae71f-3b25-523c-b399-ef203fc61915" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-203918fb-bff3-5640-9116-ee4c833a081b" :question/id #uuid "203918fb-bff3-5640-9116-ee4c833a081b" :question/math-academy-id "q-177668" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The number of rows in $A$ is not the same as the number of columns. So, it's not a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not a square matrix and ${A}^{T}\\cdot A\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4bb63660-4233-5926-a45a-b277379f4cec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4bb63660-4233-5926-a45a-b277379f4cec" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb63660-4233-5926-a45a-b277379f4cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2bad9be6-a82c-5f4f-879d-dcbfb4a2f3c1" "answer-24b180b5-cbd5-5b9a-ae2d-e655faa840d6" "answer-bae5ca7d-1994-5c77-8acf-ebf9f1ba4fb2" "answer-e09075e8-f3b4-55d6-af6b-f159bb382010" "answer-f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bad9be6-a82c-5f4f-879d-dcbfb4a2f3c1" :answer/id #uuid "2bad9be6-a82c-5f4f-879d-dcbfb4a2f3c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24b180b5-cbd5-5b9a-ae2d-e655faa840d6" :answer/id #uuid "24b180b5-cbd5-5b9a-ae2d-e655faa840d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bae5ca7d-1994-5c77-8acf-ebf9f1ba4fb2" :answer/id #uuid "bae5ca7d-1994-5c77-8acf-ebf9f1ba4fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e09075e8-f3b4-55d6-af6b-f159bb382010" :answer/id #uuid "e09075e8-f3b4-55d6-af6b-f159bb382010" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer/id #uuid "f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-340e44da-12e6-5ccb-a96a-bc97b2d0d915" :question/id #uuid "340e44da-12e6-5ccb-a96a-bc97b2d0d915" :question/math-academy-id "q-41706" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec35b09d-4f30-50dc-a52b-44c7b5d9523b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec35b09d-4f30-50dc-a52b-44c7b5d9523b" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec35b09d-4f30-50dc-a52b-44c7b5d9523b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ce8b058-46a3-588d-b171-a5e100cbc0ce" "answer-ce0c7e1d-bae0-5c82-81a4-18c4d6be60dc" "answer-be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" "answer-01ceb64c-0881-5a66-b48f-18aa35dc7f3d" "answer-af25de84-a7f8-57b5-bfd8-36f4ca12b320"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ce8b058-46a3-588d-b171-a5e100cbc0ce" :answer/id #uuid "2ce8b058-46a3-588d-b171-a5e100cbc0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce0c7e1d-bae0-5c82-81a4-18c4d6be60dc" :answer/id #uuid "ce0c7e1d-bae0-5c82-81a4-18c4d6be60dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" :answer/id #uuid "be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01ceb64c-0881-5a66-b48f-18aa35dc7f3d" :answer/id #uuid "01ceb64c-0881-5a66-b48f-18aa35dc7f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af25de84-a7f8-57b5-bfd8-36f4ca12b320" :answer/id #uuid "af25de84-a7f8-57b5-bfd8-36f4ca12b320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134242 :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131491 :answer-field/correct "answer-aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" "answer-d8eeb0b4-6fde-5e11-820c-fd3ac0790bd9" "answer-e6941f8d-a51c-5dea-b565-f989e9b10972" "answer-40815aa7-1131-5c98-b1ca-d06d1ce86431" "answer-8504229e-0026-5df9-835e-7fe9e313f2ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" :answer/id #uuid "aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8eeb0b4-6fde-5e11-820c-fd3ac0790bd9" :answer/id #uuid "d8eeb0b4-6fde-5e11-820c-fd3ac0790bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6941f8d-a51c-5dea-b565-f989e9b10972" :answer/id #uuid "e6941f8d-a51c-5dea-b565-f989e9b10972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40815aa7-1131-5c98-b1ca-d06d1ce86431" :answer/id #uuid "40815aa7-1131-5c98-b1ca-d06d1ce86431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8504229e-0026-5df9-835e-7fe9e313f2ff" :answer/id #uuid "8504229e-0026-5df9-835e-7fe9e313f2ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-36bba55d-9122-58f3-aa1e-57a8674f5e02" :question/id #uuid "36bba55d-9122-58f3-aa1e-57a8674f5e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-84245" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{8} \\\\ \\sqrt{8} & 4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}| \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ef0c785-702b-5715-b3a0-24d72749f491"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ef0c785-702b-5715-b3a0-24d72749f491" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef0c785-702b-5715-b3a0-24d72749f491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0cad6cbc-ec6f-5cde-bd6b-8dd94c36f1fc" "answer-fdf1b543-ec9d-55dc-86b7-270d6a4b27a8" "answer-5d6e869f-259c-5848-8df0-181caf97283c" "answer-40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" "answer-543c8564-bbcd-578e-9f7c-a13e39ae76f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cad6cbc-ec6f-5cde-bd6b-8dd94c36f1fc" :answer/id #uuid "0cad6cbc-ec6f-5cde-bd6b-8dd94c36f1fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdf1b543-ec9d-55dc-86b7-270d6a4b27a8" :answer/id #uuid "fdf1b543-ec9d-55dc-86b7-270d6a4b27a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d6e869f-259c-5848-8df0-181caf97283c" :answer/id #uuid "5d6e869f-259c-5848-8df0-181caf97283c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16-\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" :answer/id #uuid "40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543c8564-bbcd-578e-9f7c-a13e39ae76f5" :answer/id #uuid "543c8564-bbcd-578e-9f7c-a13e39ae76f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134244 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}| \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131503 :answer-field/correct 17592186131505 :answer-field/choices ["answer-20045821-316a-5633-acd8-365f31e8c083" "answer-9a0f3828-98fe-56d1-a565-afe9f584dd2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20045821-316a-5633-acd8-365f31e8c083" :answer/id #uuid "20045821-316a-5633-acd8-365f31e8c083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a0f3828-98fe-56d1-a565-afe9f584dd2c" :answer/id #uuid "9a0f3828-98fe-56d1-a565-afe9f584dd2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134245 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-8\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131509 :answer-field/correct 17592186131512 :answer-field/choices ["answer-36d6ba13-23fd-551d-9a3a-a0cf24d03ce2" "answer-53f9636f-f836-5a16-b4fe-9bd98143b7eb" "answer-26532a6d-633c-526a-a3c4-ae6120b78154"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36d6ba13-23fd-551d-9a3a-a0cf24d03ce2" :answer/id #uuid "36d6ba13-23fd-551d-9a3a-a0cf24d03ce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53f9636f-f836-5a16-b4fe-9bd98143b7eb" :answer/id #uuid "53f9636f-f836-5a16-b4fe-9bd98143b7eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26532a6d-633c-526a-a3c4-ae6120b78154" :answer/id #uuid "26532a6d-633c-526a-a3c4-ae6120b78154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35c37699-f2ab-5493-8b62-dd508d98be99" :question/id #uuid "35c37699-f2ab-5493-8b62-dd508d98be99" :question/math-academy-id "q-84784" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\nI. If $A=PB{P}^{-1}$ then $|det(A)|=|det(B)|$\n\nII. $PQ$ is always orthogonal\n\nIII. $2P+Q$ is **not** always orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing $|det(A)|,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|det(PB{P}^{-1})| \\\\  & =|det(PB{P}^{T})| \\\\  & =|det(P)|\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot |det({P}^{T})| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|det(B)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the product $(PQ)\\cdot (PQ)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ\\cdot (PQ)^{T} & =(PQ)\\cdot {Q}^{T}{P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(Q{Q}^{T}){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(I){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. As a counterexample, consider the following sum involving two orthogonal matrices:\n\n$$\n2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe resulting matrix is not orthogonal since, for example, the first column is not normalized.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-048ab02b-a33b-534b-a1c7-2bf319cf0b58"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-048ab02b-a33b-534b-a1c7-2bf319cf0b58" :answer-field/id #uuid "048ab02b-a33b-534b-a1c7-2bf319cf0b58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7663b203-9ab4-5d32-b8ff-e2d87fc22238" "answer-9697230b-8f6a-5224-a0f4-267b300f27ab" "answer-2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" "answer-4b086b6e-3f56-53aa-ab01-3ec1ea51c4f2" "answer-7328d2ac-ec4a-5f15-8f58-faebd2e52167"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7663b203-9ab4-5d32-b8ff-e2d87fc22238" :answer/id #uuid "7663b203-9ab4-5d32-b8ff-e2d87fc22238" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9697230b-8f6a-5224-a0f4-267b300f27ab" :answer/id #uuid "9697230b-8f6a-5224-a0f4-267b300f27ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" :answer/id #uuid "2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b086b6e-3f56-53aa-ab01-3ec1ea51c4f2" :answer/id #uuid "4b086b6e-3f56-53aa-ab01-3ec1ea51c4f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7328d2ac-ec4a-5f15-8f58-faebd2e52167" :answer/id #uuid "7328d2ac-ec4a-5f15-8f58-faebd2e52167" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4cd1f663-1b26-5239-80df-41dfbaf9dd53" :question/id #uuid "4cd1f663-1b26-5239-80df-41dfbaf9dd53" :question/math-academy-id "q-140564" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nI. ${Q}^{2}$ is orthogonal\n\nII. $Q$ is a diagonal matrix\n\nIII. $Q-I$ is invertible" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the product ${Q}^{2}\\cdot ({Q}^{2})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{2}\\cdot ({Q}^{2})^{T} & =(Q\\cdot Q)\\cdot (Q\\cdot Q)^{T} \\\\  & =(Q\\cdot Q)\\cdot ({Q}^{T}\\cdot {Q}^{T}) \\\\  & =Q\\cdot (Q\\cdot {Q}^{T})\\cdot {Q}^{T} \\\\  & =Q(I){Q}^{T} \\\\  & =Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix:\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$Q$ is an orthogonal matrix, but it is not a diagonal matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $Q=I$ be the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix. Then, \n\n$$\nQ-I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe $2\\times 2$  zero matrix, which is not an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70e8c2d5-fce1-5f92-9639-37c01a107aaf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70e8c2d5-fce1-5f92-9639-37c01a107aaf" :answer-field/id #uuid "70e8c2d5-fce1-5f92-9639-37c01a107aaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5926b979-2296-5e06-b854-1498d765329c" "answer-b7b65862-95be-58c5-99d4-ab0f73d0d20a" "answer-9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" "answer-d13939e6-36f9-5572-80e9-e753d41ea7a8" "answer-887a1bd2-c587-5e95-a0cc-d565e244878d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5926b979-2296-5e06-b854-1498d765329c" :answer/id #uuid "5926b979-2296-5e06-b854-1498d765329c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7b65862-95be-58c5-99d4-ab0f73d0d20a" :answer/id #uuid "b7b65862-95be-58c5-99d4-ab0f73d0d20a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" :answer/id #uuid "9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d13939e6-36f9-5572-80e9-e753d41ea7a8" :answer/id #uuid "d13939e6-36f9-5572-80e9-e753d41ea7a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-887a1bd2-c587-5e95-a0cc-d565e244878d" :answer/id #uuid "887a1bd2-c587-5e95-a0cc-d565e244878d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135177 :tutorial/content "Suppose we have a square $n\\times n$ matrix $Q$ with columns $\\mathbf{q}_1, \\mathbf{q}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{q}_n{:}$\n\n![](images/1b/1b69d138277cdd7ee291aaa70b81849dee28fa7112b821beaaab2235cde6c17b.svg)\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is said to be **orthogonal** if its columns $\\mathbf{q}_1, \\mathbf{q}_2, \\dots, \\mathbf{q}_n$ form an *orthonormal* set. In other words, \n\n- the columns of $Q$ must be *mutually orthogonal*, and\n\n- they must all be *unit* vectors.\n\nFor instance, the matrix \n![](images/8c/8c5cdeffc5e91988c140e53623b252c100f86e573a4f2c5a761b5e7667cce9ef.svg) \nis orthogonal since its columns \n\n![](images/87/874cd61d37f79fc732f36b7b3a2578b4957dde1a364522674cb3c93fe4c50ae8.svg)\n\nform an orthonormal set $\\left\\{ {\\color{black}\\mathbf{q}_1}, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{q}_2} \\right\\}.$ To see this, note the following:\n\n- The vectors $\\mathbf q_1$ and $\\mathbf q_2$ are orthogonal, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Both $\\mathbf q_1$ and $\\mathbf q_2$ are unit vectors, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||{q}_{1}|{|}^{2} & ={q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||{q}_{2}|{|}^{2} & ={q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135182 :tutorial/content "Checking that the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal set is a fair amount of work. Thankfully, we have the following theorem to make our lives easier: \n\n*A matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if*\n\n$$\nQ \\cdot Q^T = Q^T \\cdot Q = I\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $Q^T$ denotes the transpose of $Q.$  It's the matrix we get when we interchange the rows and columns of $Q.$\n\n- To verify that a matrix is orthogonal in practice, we only need to check that $Q \\, Q^T = I.$\n\nLet's see an example of applying this theorem." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135179 :tutorial/content "Recall the following theorem:\n\n*A matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if*\n\n$$\nQ \\cdot {\\color{blue}{Q^T}} = {\\color{blue}{Q^T}} \\cdot Q = I.\n$$\n\nNow, recall that for $Q$ to be invertible, there must exist a matrix $Q^{-1}$ such that\n\n$$\nQ \\cdot {\\color{blue}{Q^{-1}}} = {\\color{blue}{Q^{-1}}} \\cdot Q = I.\n$$\n\nBy comparing the two equations above, we can deduce the following:\n\n- Every orthogonal matrix $Q$ is invertible, and\n\n- the inverse of an orthogonal matrix $Q$ is ${\\color{blue}{Q^T}},$ that is\n\n$$\nQ^{-1} = Q^T.\n$$\n\nThese properties explain why orthogonal matrices are desirable. We can always find the inverse of an orthogonal matrix, and we can quickly compute the inverse by simply transposing the original matrix." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133992 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f3cfd772-56f0-5f8d-9613-e2a636e3f6c4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3cfd772-56f0-5f8d-9613-e2a636e3f6c4" :question/id #uuid "f3cfd772-56f0-5f8d-9613-e2a636e3f6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-133802" :question/problem "Aaron, Beatrice, and Chetna have each baked $2$ cherry pies and $3$ apple pies for the sale. In total, they baked{{field-1}}\npies." :question/worked-solution "We need to write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of pies.\n\nSince each of them baked $2$ cherry pies and $3$ apple pies, the number of pies each person made is:\n\n$$\n{{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{cherry pies}}+{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{apple pies}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person made this number of pies, and there are $3$ people, we must multiply the number of pies by $3.$ Therefore, the total number of pies is:\n\n$$\n{{(2+3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+3)\\times 3 & =(2+3)\\times 3 \\\\  & =5\\times 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n5\\times 3=15\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35121271-51e1-5687-872f-b1f42af21c50"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35121271-51e1-5687-872f-b1f42af21c50" :answer-field/id #uuid "35121271-51e1-5687-872f-b1f42af21c50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-01c5ab47-14e9-5e2b-9447-8973112061ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01c5ab47-14e9-5e2b-9447-8973112061ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01c5ab47-14e9-5e2b-9447-8973112061ff" :answer/id #uuid "01c5ab47-14e9-5e2b-9447-8973112061ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059859 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7dffbb18-69db-5548-9e20-8e99e6ab3d7c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7dffbb18-69db-5548-9e20-8e99e6ab3d7c" :question/id #uuid "7dffbb18-69db-5548-9e20-8e99e6ab3d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-133803" :question/problem "At the bake sale, there are $12$ tables with $18$ cakes at each table. Therefore, there are{{field-1}}\ncakes in total." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total number of cakes, we need to multiply $12$ by $18.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 8=96\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 10=120\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}96+120=216\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12\\times 18=216.$\n\nTherefore, there are $216$ cakes in total." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fac530a4-31cf-5ed3-9ace-18c2b43e1fd3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fac530a4-31cf-5ed3-9ace-18c2b43e1fd3" :answer-field/id #uuid "fac530a4-31cf-5ed3-9ace-18c2b43e1fd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f5de1019-e44b-51c8-b1d6-811e595007cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5de1019-e44b-51c8-b1d6-811e595007cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5de1019-e44b-51c8-b1d6-811e595007cb" :answer/id #uuid "f5de1019-e44b-51c8-b1d6-811e595007cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "216" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43bd5eed-55d7-5512-b491-efa9bc5b652f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-43bd5eed-55d7-5512-b491-efa9bc5b652f" :question/id #uuid "43bd5eed-55d7-5512-b491-efa9bc5b652f" :question/math-academy-id "q-133804" :question/problem "If a total of $9$ people made all the cakes for the sale, and each person made the same number of cakes, then they each made{{field-1}}\ncakes." :question/worked-solution "We know that there are $216$ cakes in total. So, each person made $216÷9$ cakes.\n\nWe start by writing down the question using long division notation:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{2\\,\\phantom{|}1\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that $2$ (the number of hundreds in $216$) is less than the divisor $9.$ Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{2\\,\\phantom{|}1\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$↓$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $21÷9=2\\,\\text{R}\\,3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over tens: $2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $9\\times 2=18$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $21-18=3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Bring down: $6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNext, we consider the ones:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{2\\,\\phantom{|}1\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $36÷9=4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over ones: $4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $9\\times 4=36$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $36-36=0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get the remainder $0$, so the division is done.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n216÷9=24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9df461e3-1782-571c-a80a-bda5b40ea94b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9df461e3-1782-571c-a80a-bda5b40ea94b" :answer-field/id #uuid "9df461e3-1782-571c-a80a-bda5b40ea94b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5ef72a28-0a22-52df-87fd-e897740c3fad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ef72a28-0a22-52df-87fd-e897740c3fad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ef72a28-0a22-52df-87fd-e897740c3fad" :answer/id #uuid "5ef72a28-0a22-52df-87fd-e897740c3fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073698 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fb3049fb-d3cf-5bb1-b456-516f986d2262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb3049fb-d3cf-5bb1-b456-516f986d2262" :question/id #uuid "fb3049fb-d3cf-5bb1-b456-516f986d2262" :question/math-academy-id "q-133805" :question/problem "Darryl buys $2$ cherry pies and $\\frac{4}{3}$ of an apple pie. How much pie did Darryl buy in total? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nDarryl bought\n{{field-1}}\npies." :question/worked-solution "To find out how much pie Darryl bought, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n2+\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nTo add $2$ and $\\frac{4}{3},$ we need to express the whole number $2$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $3.$\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $3$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 3}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{6}{3}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{6+4}{3}=\\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n10÷3=3\\,\\text{R}\\,1=3\\,\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Darryl bought $3\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ pies." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e6b9edd-f6dd-500c-8e8b-88adbe16a5bd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e6b9edd-f6dd-500c-8e8b-88adbe16a5bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6b9edd-f6dd-500c-8e8b-88adbe16a5bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e8784ea2-9999-5a27-973c-a5d014b476bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8784ea2-9999-5a27-973c-a5d014b476bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8784ea2-9999-5a27-973c-a5d014b476bb" :answer/id #uuid "e8784ea2-9999-5a27-973c-a5d014b476bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aa1b20cc-21de-5821-9525-46da1d460229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa1b20cc-21de-5821-9525-46da1d460229" :question/id #uuid "aa1b20cc-21de-5821-9525-46da1d460229" :question/math-academy-id "q-133806" :question/problem "Of the $2$ of Darryl's cherry pies, Ellen takes $\\frac{5}{7}$ of a pie. As a mixed number, Darryl has{{field-1}}\ncherry pies left." :question/worked-solution "To find out how much cherry pie Darryl has left, we must calculate the difference $2-\\frac{5}{7}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{5}{7}$ from $2,$ we need to express the whole number $2$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $7.$\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $7$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{1\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{7}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{7}-\\frac{5}{7}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{7}-\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{14-5}{7}=\\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n9÷7=1\\,\\text{R}\\,2=1\\,\\frac{2}{7}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Darryl has $1\\,\\frac{2}{7}$ cherry pies left." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7fe34f7c-29fe-5043-b266-5728c91eaf26"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7fe34f7c-29fe-5043-b266-5728c91eaf26" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fe34f7c-29fe-5043-b266-5728c91eaf26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0910b7ee-a05f-5aa4-98df-c9e93c234cdd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0910b7ee-a05f-5aa4-98df-c9e93c234cdd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0910b7ee-a05f-5aa4-98df-c9e93c234cdd" :answer/id #uuid "0910b7ee-a05f-5aa4-98df-c9e93c234cdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198431 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0a57b3c9-03a4-52de-a46c-64a4643241ad"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a57b3c9-03a4-52de-a46c-64a4643241ad" :question/id #uuid "0a57b3c9-03a4-52de-a46c-64a4643241ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-133807" :question/problem "After Ellen takes her bite of Darryl's cherry pie, Darryl's remaining cherry pie is{{field-1}}\nthan Darryl's remaining apple pie because  $1\\frac{2}{7}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Darryl has $1\\frac{2}{7}$ cherry pies and $\\frac{4}{3}$ apple pies remaining.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $7\\times 3=21.$\n\nTo put $1\\frac{2}{7}$ over a denominator of $21,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n1\\frac{2}{7}=\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{7\\times 3}=\\frac{27}{21}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{4}{3}$ over a denominator of $21,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{4\\times 7}{3\\times 7}=\\frac{28}{21}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{27}{21}$ and $\\frac{28}{21}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $27<28,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{21}<\\frac{28}{21}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Ellen takes her bite of Darryl's cherry pie, Darryl's remaining cherry pie is $<$ than Darryl's remaining apple pie because $1\\frac{2}{7}<\\frac{4}{3}.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d74ba4e3-6609-57f0-a5d9-9c0bee314a02" "answer-field-c37e0a1c-7302-5dcb-9393-66c1caaf2c23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d74ba4e3-6609-57f0-a5d9-9c0bee314a02" :answer-field/id #uuid "d74ba4e3-6609-57f0-a5d9-9c0bee314a02" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0d6e4d0e-a01c-54ee-9889-0986a07f14e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d6e4d0e-a01c-54ee-9889-0986a07f14e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6e4d0e-a01c-54ee-9889-0986a07f14e2" :answer/id #uuid "0d6e4d0e-a01c-54ee-9889-0986a07f14e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "less" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c37e0a1c-7302-5dcb-9393-66c1caaf2c23" :answer-field/id #uuid "c37e0a1c-7302-5dcb-9393-66c1caaf2c23" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c7a4f173-8537-52f7-8940-6a99ceeca293" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7a4f173-8537-52f7-8940-6a99ceeca293"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7a4f173-8537-52f7-8940-6a99ceeca293" :answer/id #uuid "c7a4f173-8537-52f7-8940-6a99ceeca293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142796 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7d63aa21-54c3-5793-bdf0-1f7c092e61d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7d63aa21-54c3-5793-bdf0-1f7c092e61d0" :question/id #uuid "7d63aa21-54c3-5793-bdf0-1f7c092e61d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-133808" :question/problem "Darryl gives $\\frac{2}{5}$ of his apple pies to his daughter. What fraction of a whole pie does Darryl's daughter have?\n\n*Remember that Darryl bought $\\frac{4}{3}$ of an apple pie.*\n\nDarryl's daughter has\n{{field-1}}\nof a pie." :question/worked-solution "We know that Darryl has $\\frac{4}{3}$ of an apple pie.\n\nTo calculate the fraction of a whole pie that Darryl's daughter has, we need to multiply $\\frac{2}{5}$ by $\\frac{4}{3}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{2\\times 4}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{8}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Darry's daughter have $\\frac{8}{15}$ of a pie." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb066ac7-3e74-53e0-a852-3680d4d4d5ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb066ac7-3e74-53e0-a852-3680d4d4d5ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb066ac7-3e74-53e0-a852-3680d4d4d5ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b6818a4d-d22e-50c1-a69c-bc909b29e84f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b6818a4d-d22e-50c1-a69c-bc909b29e84f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6818a4d-d22e-50c1-a69c-bc909b29e84f" :answer/id #uuid "b6818a4d-d22e-50c1-a69c-bc909b29e84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "multistep-8ce01573-84d9-5c59-8210-9379d68685c7" :multistep/id #uuid "8ce01573-84d9-5c59-8210-9379d68685c7" :mult