"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7db8904e-ed60-51dc-86e9-b75d6a4fd533" :answer/id #uuid "7db8904e-ed60-51dc-86e9-b75d6a4fd533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa8b4c4c-e3b9-5ca8-85ef-9c187ca62865" :answer/id #uuid "fa8b4c4c-e3b9-5ca8-85ef-9c187ca62865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c1b2818-d887-5177-b85a-26738407f7be" :answer/id #uuid "6c1b2818-d887-5177-b85a-26738407f7be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-345f5bfc-41f6-5f56-8e7f-360d75f818bf" :answer/id #uuid "345f5bfc-41f6-5f56-8e7f-360d75f818bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56f50180-a7e4-5a28-b023-07cf58f2b323" :answer/id #uuid "56f50180-a7e4-5a28-b023-07cf58f2b323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e0ee09c-000d-5a57-8be4-46c85b5f432d" :question/id #uuid "8e0ee09c-000d-5a57-8be4-46c85b5f432d" :question/math-academy-id "q-213447" :question/problem "$\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{7\\sqrt{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{2}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{7\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{7\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{7\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{7\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{14} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2\\cdot 3}}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cdfbed6e-c86a-586c-98ee-e7940e24e99d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cdfbed6e-c86a-586c-98ee-e7940e24e99d" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdfbed6e-c86a-586c-98ee-e7940e24e99d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-00ecdfe3-9b08-5fb1-b2c4-f7c14a6803f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95721d58-634e-5313-b505-bcce7a586680" "answer-00ecdfe3-9b08-5fb1-b2c4-f7c14a6803f5" "answer-7d52b5db-b014-5690-b1f1-62a55cd0fe0d" "answer-3d1ca554-efa8-56a0-b421-8583c61a580d" "answer-4b832563-57cf-5661-a855-3ef11dd96c9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95721d58-634e-5313-b505-bcce7a586680" :answer/id #uuid "95721d58-634e-5313-b505-bcce7a586680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ecdfe3-9b08-5fb1-b2c4-f7c14a6803f5" :answer/id #uuid "00ecdfe3-9b08-5fb1-b2c4-f7c14a6803f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d52b5db-b014-5690-b1f1-62a55cd0fe0d" :answer/id #uuid "7d52b5db-b014-5690-b1f1-62a55cd0fe0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d1ca554-efa8-56a0-b421-8583c61a580d" :answer/id #uuid "3d1ca554-efa8-56a0-b421-8583c61a580d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b832563-57cf-5661-a855-3ef11dd96c9b" :answer/id #uuid "4b832563-57cf-5661-a855-3ef11dd96c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b78114a3-4df5-565e-b851-3da12ef84e72" :question/id #uuid "b78114a3-4df5-565e-b851-3da12ef84e72" :question/math-academy-id "q-212957" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{2}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $45$ has a perfect square factor $(9).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{45}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{45} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{5\\cdot 2}}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1d543d6-08df-55d3-9489-c58386a70208"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1d543d6-08df-55d3-9489-c58386a70208" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d543d6-08df-55d3-9489-c58386a70208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" "answer-95572b10-05b0-5990-8a00-0db90e625610" "answer-d8fe7281-679d-5b48-bbf3-31ebcfb49f43" "answer-224545ba-26f7-5316-81be-067cbbabb927" "answer-34bc50aa-c243-52a5-824d-c7eb5489c515"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" :answer/id #uuid "ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95572b10-05b0-5990-8a00-0db90e625610" :answer/id #uuid "95572b10-05b0-5990-8a00-0db90e625610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8fe7281-679d-5b48-bbf3-31ebcfb49f43" :answer/id #uuid "d8fe7281-679d-5b48-bbf3-31ebcfb49f43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-224545ba-26f7-5316-81be-067cbbabb927" :answer/id #uuid "224545ba-26f7-5316-81be-067cbbabb927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34bc50aa-c243-52a5-824d-c7eb5489c515" :answer/id #uuid "34bc50aa-c243-52a5-824d-c7eb5489c515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106176 :question/problem "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{8}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{8}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{8}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $8$ has a perfect square factor $(4).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{8}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3\\cdot 2}}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102932 :answer-field/correct 17592186102934 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106175 :question/problem "$\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{3}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{3}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $8$ has a perfect square factor $(4).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{8}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2\\cdot 3}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102926 :answer-field/correct 17592186102931 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f188433-9891-58cb-8279-ce3757720a45" :question/id #uuid "0f188433-9891-58cb-8279-ce3757720a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-212962" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{27}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{27}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{27}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{27}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{27}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{27}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{27}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{27}}{27} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $27$ has a perfect square factor $(9).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{27}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{27}}{27} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}}{27} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{27} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5\\cdot 3}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91476299-4b29-5a42-b053-5f639a6f9a67"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91476299-4b29-5a42-b053-5f639a6f9a67" :answer-field/id #uuid "91476299-4b29-5a42-b053-5f639a6f9a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee2f8dbe-b7d6-5ec4-b856-e83b6f6604fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee2f8dbe-b7d6-5ec4-b856-e83b6f6604fc" "answer-08834aad-855d-5f34-a2a9-88ed02914db0" "answer-293577e5-ec0c-5386-8f6a-ae3dd3b5a516" "answer-c3b6e228-4f64-52aa-aa6f-451fa1f7180f" "answer-c3a892be-98c8-518b-878d-988ded593924"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee2f8dbe-b7d6-5ec4-b856-e83b6f6604fc" :answer/id #uuid "ee2f8dbe-b7d6-5ec4-b856-e83b6f6604fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08834aad-855d-5f34-a2a9-88ed02914db0" :answer/id #uuid "08834aad-855d-5f34-a2a9-88ed02914db0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-293577e5-ec0c-5386-8f6a-ae3dd3b5a516" :answer/id #uuid "293577e5-ec0c-5386-8f6a-ae3dd3b5a516" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3b6e228-4f64-52aa-aa6f-451fa1f7180f" :answer/id #uuid "c3b6e228-4f64-52aa-aa6f-451fa1f7180f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3a892be-98c8-518b-878d-988ded593924" :answer/id #uuid "c3a892be-98c8-518b-878d-988ded593924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107169 :tutorial/content "Whenever we have a fraction that contains a square root in the denominator, such as $\\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},$ we often want to find an equivalent fraction that has no square root in the denominator.\n\nTo find this equivalent fraction, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the square root in the denominator. This process is known as **rationalizing the denominator**.\n\nFor example, for the fraction $\\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},$ we can remove the square root from the denominator by multiplying both the numerator and denominator by the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, when we rationalize the denominator in the fraction  $\\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},$ we get the equivalent fraction $\\dfrac{3 \\sqrt{2} }{ 2 }$ that has no square root in the denominator." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105972 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186062173 :answer-field/choices 17592186062176] [:db/retract 17592186062173 :answer-field/choices 17592186062177] [:db/retract 17592186062173 :answer-field/choices 17592186062178] [:db/retract 17592186062173 :answer-field/choices 17592186062174] [:db/retract 17592186062173 :answer-field/choices 17592186062175] [:db/retract 17592186062209 :answer-field/choices 17592186062210] [:db/retract 17592186062209 :answer-field/choices 17592186062211] [:db/retract 17592186062209 :answer-field/choices 17592186062212] [:db/retract 17592186062209 :answer-field/choices 17592186062213] [:db/retract 17592186062209 :answer-field/choices 17592186062214] {:db/id 17592186064686 :question/problem "Factor the expression $16{a}^{2}-81.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{a}^{2}-81 & =(4a)^{2}-{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a)^{2}-{9}^{2} & =(4a+9)(4a-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062173 :answer-field/correct "answer-51172389-9c15-5caa-bf7e-b95637b65d2e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73e7769f-fc92-5de8-8c10-550b71e31703" "answer-24bb8047-0ff3-5b85-aee9-2e6ac88d6e1d" "answer-9035e54c-8039-5816-9bcf-cf8e910bf09e" "answer-51172389-9c15-5caa-bf7e-b95637b65d2e" "answer-28b71172-7a45-5d09-98d1-64ccf6b8bfda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73e7769f-fc92-5de8-8c10-550b71e31703" :answer/id #uuid "73e7769f-fc92-5de8-8c10-550b71e31703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2a-3)(2a+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24bb8047-0ff3-5b85-aee9-2e6ac88d6e1d" :answer/id #uuid "24bb8047-0ff3-5b85-aee9-2e6ac88d6e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2a-3)(2a-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9035e54c-8039-5816-9bcf-cf8e910bf09e" :answer/id #uuid "9035e54c-8039-5816-9bcf-cf8e910bf09e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4a+9)(4a+9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51172389-9c15-5caa-bf7e-b95637b65d2e" :answer/id #uuid "51172389-9c15-5caa-bf7e-b95637b65d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4a-9)(4a+9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28b71172-7a45-5d09-98d1-64ccf6b8bfda" :answer/id #uuid "28b71172-7a45-5d09-98d1-64ccf6b8bfda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4a-9)(4a-9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064692 :question/problem "Express $4{e}^{2}-16{f}^{2}$ as a product of two binomials." :question/worked-solution "We factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{2}-16{f}^{2} & = \\\\ (2e)^{2}-(4f)^{2} & = \\\\ (2e-4f)(2e+4f) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062209 :answer-field/correct "answer-58d24321-d687-5666-b444-c67333ddf888" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b13e591a-bf5d-5ccb-bebd-477bcfb2fa24" "answer-58d24321-d687-5666-b444-c67333ddf888" "answer-883f814c-6c18-5941-967b-2ebea351df17" "answer-a2d7f83e-938d-58ce-b03e-2aa0fbe0f394" "answer-fdc225a0-8ce8-5951-977f-0f5267f0a478"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b13e591a-bf5d-5ccb-bebd-477bcfb2fa24" :answer/id #uuid "b13e591a-bf5d-5ccb-bebd-477bcfb2fa24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2e+4f)(2e+4f)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58d24321-d687-5666-b444-c67333ddf888" :answer/id #uuid "58d24321-d687-5666-b444-c67333ddf888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2e-4f)(2e+4f)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-883f814c-6c18-5941-967b-2ebea351df17" :answer/id #uuid "883f814c-6c18-5941-967b-2ebea351df17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2e-4f)(2e-4f)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2d7f83e-938d-58ce-b03e-2aa0fbe0f394" :answer/id #uuid "a2d7f83e-938d-58ce-b03e-2aa0fbe0f394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e-2f)(e+2f)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdc225a0-8ce8-5951-977f-0f5267f0a478" :answer/id #uuid "fdc225a0-8ce8-5951-977f-0f5267f0a478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e-2f)(e-2f)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064328 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7a010f5a-cc94-5c4d-81d2-4c21165ae9ab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7a010f5a-cc94-5c4d-81d2-4c21165ae9ab" :question/id #uuid "7a010f5a-cc94-5c4d-81d2-4c21165ae9ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-44102" :question/problem "$81-{x}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the expression as 