activity/title "Factoring Differences of Squares" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048928 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-13e0558d-c68a-56fe-97cc-a967ca46bd21" "step-8a3fd681-fb58-5e69-96b1-2127582ffe4f" "step-2738148b-cedf-57d8-ae04-d09d72e66898"] :activity/first-step "step-13e0558d-c68a-56fe-97cc-a967ca46bd21" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-13e0558d-c68a-56fe-97cc-a967ca46bd21" :step/id #uuid "13e0558d-c68a-56fe-97cc-a967ca46bd21" :step/content 17592186064686 :step/next "step-8a3fd681-fb58-5e69-96b1-2127582ffe4f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a3fd681-fb58-5e69-96b1-2127582ffe4f" :step/id #uuid "8a3fd681-fb58-5e69-96b1-2127582ffe4f" :step/content 17592186064692 :step/next "step-2738148b-cedf-57d8-ae04-d09d72e66898" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2738148b-cedf-57d8-ae04-d09d72e66898" :step/id #uuid "2738148b-cedf-57d8-ae04-d09d72e66898" :step/content "question-7a010f5a-cc94-5c4d-81d2-4c21165ae9ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186118250 :answer-field/choices 17592186118251] [:db/retract 17592186118250 :answer-field/choices 17592186118252] [:db/retract 17592186118250 :answer-field/choices 17592186118253] [:db/retract 17592186118250 :answer-field/choices 17592186118254] [:db/retract 17592186118250 :answer-field/choices 17592186118255] {:db/id 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1bd4e151-d470-5686-8d26-76a2f90fc9ab" "question-72798764-caa8-5165-8cde-e9f5d6b201ad"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120356 :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=(t+2)\\,i+(\\sqrt{2}t-2)\\,j-t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=2t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{s}{2}+2)i+(\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}-2)j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =(\\frac{s+4}{2})i+(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s-4}{2})j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s+4}{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s-4}{2})j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{2})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118250 :answer-field/correct "answer-cbc40c26-154e-540c-b167-bab2ca6ddfbc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e226f754-b94d-52bf-a072-a6d3d6155d75" "answer-8516513a-8c46-5d5b-9c96-4f7574d94c8f" "answer-cbc40c26-154e-540c-b167-bab2ca6ddfbc" "answer-808c3d96-e051-54b7-abc8-f503d0f4399f" "answer-c575acd8-bd34-5084-ac96-b6d573032127"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e226f754-b94d-52bf-a072-a6d3d6155d75" :answer/id #uuid "e226f754-b94d-52bf-a072-a6d3d6155d75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j-\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8516513a-8c46-5d5b-9c96-4f7574d94c8f" :answer/id #uuid "8516513a-8c46-5d5b-9c96-4f7574d94c8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbc40c26-154e-540c-b167-bab2ca6ddfbc" :answer/id #uuid "cbc40c26-154e-540c-b167-bab2ca6ddfbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-808c3d96-e051-54b7-abc8-f503d0f4399f" :answer/id #uuid "808c3d96-e051-54b7-abc8-f503d0f4399f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c575acd8-bd34-5084-ac96-b6d573032127" :answer/id #uuid "c575acd8-bd34-5084-ac96-b6d573032127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{s}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{2}\\,j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1bd4e151-d470-5686-8d26-76a2f90fc9ab" :question/id #uuid "1bd4e151-d470-5686-8d26-76a2f90fc9ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-127705" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\sqrt{5},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=3t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=3t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-589092fa-ff4f-5507-8f77-fd531d740c3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-589092fa-ff4f-5507-8f77-fd531d740c3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "589092fa-ff4f-5507-8f77-fd531d740c3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9bc2226e-ee70-510d-bc66-ff349daea915" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9bc2226e-ee70-510d-bc66-ff349daea915" "answer-b21b8788-0001-5c14-9230-a8c727b9b478" "answer-00d50bca-92fb-55a8-95fa-679d33e3532a" "answer-714608fd-7b16-5349-b7e9-a6f3edf1f4dd" "answer-48d183bf-007f-5b04-a232-41002099c1e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bc2226e-ee70-510d-bc66-ff349daea915" :answer/id #uuid "9bc2226e-ee70-510d-bc66-ff349daea915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b21b8788-0001-5c14-9230-a8c727b9b478" :answer/id #uuid "b21b8788-0001-5c14-9230-a8c727b9b478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\sqrt{7},\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00d50bca-92fb-55a8-95fa-679d33e3532a" :answer/id #uuid "00d50bca-92fb-55a8-95fa-679d33e3532a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-714608fd-7b16-5349-b7e9-a6f3edf1f4dd" :answer/id #uuid "714608fd-7b16-5349-b7e9-a6f3edf1f4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48d183bf-007f-5b04-a232-41002099c1e6" :answer/id #uuid "48d183bf-007f-5b04-a232-41002099c1e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T(s)=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-72798764-caa8-5165-8cde-e9f5d6b201ad" :question/id #uuid "72798764-caa8-5165-8cde-e9f5d6b201ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-129738" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}(1+t)^{3/2},\\,t,\\,\\frac{4}{3}(1-t)^{3/2}⟩,$ $-1\\le t\\le 1,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=3t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=3t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{(1-\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{s}{3}},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{s}{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{3+s},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3-s}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72fd9bc1-8b09-5167-a079-9e30ee96793c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72fd9bc1-8b09-5167-a079-9e30ee96793c" :answer-field/id #uuid "72fd9bc1-8b09-5167-a079-9e30ee96793c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-320f4aa0-708b-5ab1-987b-059bdbf94bf6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb9fb01c-a4f1-5042-9365-5d57dca9b009" "answer-84627639-2fe8-58d5-8d64-3bfd4d45a9b1" "answer-552a44df-a03e-5e37-b037-66869b26d4bc" "answer-f6f69e6c-4b